# Modern JS & TS Patterns for API Layer

## 1. Type Safety & Generics
- Avoid `any` at all costs.
- Use explicit return types on API fetcher functions (`Promise<ResponseType>`).
- Define `queryKey` tuples with `as const`.
- Handle unknown payloads with structured interfaces or `Record<string, unknown>`.

## 2. Asynchronous Patterns & Error Handling
- Use `async/await` syntax instead of promise chaining (`.then().catch()`).
- Always bubble HTTP exceptions as typed `ApiError` instances.
- Never swallow errors silently without logging via `logger.error`.

## 3. Immutability & Clean State
- Treat React Query cache as immutable.
- Use pure selector functions (`select: (data) => ...`) to transform API responses into UI-ready models.
- Keep helper functions deterministic and free of side effects.
